{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return (G.L. c. 186 § 15B)","requirement":"A landlord may not require a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% yearly interest, give receipts and a condition statement, and return it within 30 days of move-out.","key_value":"1 month's rent; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"All leases and tenancies of residential real property in Massachusetts.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest liability for a deposit does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution; granting a mortgage is not a transfer of interest.","penalty":"Landlord forfeits any right to retain the deposit and is liable for three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof;  provided, however, that the lessor may deduct from such security deposit for the following:","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on amounts collectible at the start of a tenancy (G.L. c. 186 § 15B)","requirement":"A landlord or agent may not require a tenant or applicant to pay upfront more than the first month's rent, the last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and the cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"1st month + last month rent + 1 month deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Any lease or tenancy of residential real property; applies to a lessor or the lessor's agent.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:\n(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and,\n(ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,\n(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit option must be offered without regard to income or credit score (G.L. c. 186 § 15B)","requirement":"A landlord who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer that option to every prospective tenant whose application is approved, regardless of income, credit score or household size, and may not consider those factors in setting the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors of residential real property who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

